=== DEFECTS FOUND AND FIXED ===

1. N-10 CONFORMANCE GAP (found during extraction, before coding).
   N-10 requires every failure record to identify six things. FailureRecord
   carried only three: the engine survived merely as a substring of object_id,
   and the invocation and attempted inputs were unrecoverable. Confirmed
   empirically against a live orchestrated failure (inputs ev-1/ev-2 lost).
   Fixed additively: optional engine/cycle_id/invocation_index/input_ids
   fields defaulting to None/(), populated by orchestration, plus
   satisfies_n10_attribution reporting conformance rather than assuming it.
   All four existing producers unchanged.

2. HOSTILE EXCEPTION RENDERING ABORTED THE CYCLE.
   The failure detail was built with an f-string, calling str(exc). An engine
   whose exception has a raising __str__ made that call raise from inside the
   except handler; the new exception propagated out of run_cycle, the entire
   cycle record was discarded, remaining work was never attempted and the
   failure was never recorded. Exactly the "one engine fails mid-batch,
   leaving inconsistent state" mode PKP v2 4.12 names, breaching N-10 and AC2.
   Fixed with _describe_exception(), which reads the type from the class and
   can never itself raise. KeyboardInterrupt/SystemExit deliberately excluded
   -- they are control signals, and recording one as an engine failure would
   misattribute a shutdown.

3. A RAISING FAILURE STORE MADE EVERY FAILURE INVISIBLE.
   failure_store.record() was called unguarded, so a store fault propagated
   out of run_cycle and destroyed the whole cycle record: total masking, the
   worst N-10 outcome. Fixed by guarding the write, keeping the record on the
   CycleRecord regardless, and recording the persistence fault itself as a
   FAILURE-STORE-UNAVAILABLE record so it is not swallowed either. No retry
   [M-36 policy half OPEN]. The per-cycle fault list is reset at cycle START,
   which a mutation proved load-bearing: without it an aborted cycle's stale
   fault is misattributed to the next cycle.

=== SPECIFICATION CONFLICT RECORDED, NOT RESOLVED ===
N-10's header and TIMELINE.md state that N-10 closes M-36, but PKP v2 s13
still lists M-36 as open and marker-crosswalk.md records M-36 as compound:
"policy + representation". N-10's Decision section addresses representation
only and states no retry/skip/halt/compensate rule. The POLICY half is
therefore treated as OPEN and failed closed: no retry, skip, halt,
compensation or recovery is implemented. Documented in
validation/T01.6.3-specification.md section 7 and in the module header.
